column7:
This has happened to me several times. Especially in combination with the fact that C++ does not guarantee floating point operations happen the same every time... Argh. So it is unwise to do things like<p><pre><code>  bool operator()(Foo const& a, Foo const& b) const {
    return a.some_float_func() < b.some_float_func();
  }
</code></pre>
if some_float_func does floating point operations rather than just returning a stored value.
